cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite this concept DOI for the evolving powerfit project. For the numerical
  evidence used by the manuscript, cite the version-specific powerfit v1.0.0
  reference below together with pyvoro2 0.6.3. Also cite the associated
  manuscript or article when its publication identifier is available.
title: >-
  powerfit: reproducibility materials for inverse fitting of
  power-diagram weights from pairwise separator data
type: software
version: 2.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Chernyshov
    given-names: Ivan Yu.
    affiliation: Independent researcher
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4452-2025"
repository-code: https://github.com/DeloneCommons/powerfit
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19673557
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19673557
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Version 2.0.0 revised manuscript source, figure and build helpers, and frozen experimental
  protocols, inputs, and results for inverse fitting of power-diagram weights
  from pairwise separator data. The experimental evidence is preserved in
  powerfit v1.0.0, while this concept DOI identifies the evolving project. The
  MIT license applies to first-party materials; bundled third-party artifacts
  retain their upstream licenses and notices.
keywords:
  - power diagram
  - Laguerre tessellation
  - inverse problem
  - graph Laplacian
  - reproducibility
